                <pb facs="0540" n="454" sameAs="frus:frus1927v01/pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">863.51/847: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washburn</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-10-28T11:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 28,
                                1927—11 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>20. Your 54, September 20, 10 a.m. and despatch 1532, September 20. In opinion of
                    law officers of this Government, the Secretary of the Treasury has no power to
                    act further under the Joint Resolution approved April 6, 1922, and a new
                    enabling act of Congress would be necessary to enable him to take the suggested
                    action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Olds</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
